WEBVTT

00:02.160 --> 00:03.560
Tell the envoy

00:03.760 --> 00:05.640
Great Xuan can offer Yan Dong

00:05.720 --> 00:06.560
Rice seeds

00:06.640 --> 00:07.720
Money and grain

00:07.800 --> 00:08.720
Silk

00:08.800 --> 00:09.400
Tea

00:09.480 --> 00:10.160
Armor

00:10.280 --> 00:11.680
Anything

00:12.480 --> 00:13.880
But no princess

00:16.080 --> 00:17.240
Great Xuan

00:17.320 --> 00:18.680
Does not marry daughters out

00:18.760 --> 00:20.160
Yes

00:36.160 --> 00:37.120
Your Majesty

00:37.200 --> 00:39.200
The Yan envoy has already left

00:41.440 --> 00:42.560
Your Majesty is benevolent

00:42.640 --> 00:44.080
It is the princess's fortune

00:44.160 --> 00:45.560
The people's fortune

00:46.680 --> 00:48.080
These words

00:48.200 --> 00:49.867
You tell the Crown Prince

00:52.000 --> 01:12.000
In the twentieth year of Longwu, the Grand Dan Khagan led fifty envoys on behalf of Yarkand's fine warhorses, yet the sovereign of Yan and Qi offered only ten thousand steeds, leaving both sides locked in a fierce dispute.

